00:41:11.270 --> 00:41:14.810
I was backstage on a phone, so I didn't see it go down.

877
00:41:14.990 --> 00:41:18.310
Angela, do you remember, was there like a mattress or something that they landed on?

878
00:41:18.430 --> 00:41:20.470
There was a big blue squishy thing.

879
00:41:20.630 --> 00:41:21.370
You know what I mean?

880
00:41:21.450 --> 00:41:22.290
A big blue square.

881
00:41:22.290 --> 00:41:24.650
It looked like a gymnastics kind of mat, right?

882
00:41:24.890 --> 00:41:25.110
Yeah.

883
00:41:25.370 --> 00:41:26.490
But it was so funny.

884
00:41:26.690 --> 00:41:32.010
I have to imagine John lost it because John did not do well in scenes like that, especially

885
00:41:32.010 --> 00:41:32.970
with Steve Blake.

886
00:41:33.070 --> 00:41:33.490
I don't.

887
00:41:33.650 --> 00:41:36.210
My memory of it is they didn't do it very many times.

888
00:41:36.410 --> 00:41:36.630
Okay.

889
00:41:37.790 --> 00:41:39.430
Well, now we're into the episode.

890
00:41:39.730 --> 00:41:40.590
It's Ethics Day.

891
00:41:40.950 --> 00:41:43.530
Holly has passed out a form everyone has to fill out.

892
00:41:43.730 --> 00:41:45.430
She's going to be taking this seriously.

893
00:41:45.690 --> 00:41:46.250
She is.

894
00:41:46.390 --> 00:41:49.830
She explains that she is going to be running her first meeting.

895
00:41:50.430 --> 00:41:51.650
But don't worry.

896
00:41:51.670 --> 00:41:54.230
We talked about this with Amy Ryan.

897
00:41:55.050 --> 00:42:00.290
Michael's going to help her out, and they're going to start it off with their version of

898
00:42:00.290 --> 00:42:01.530
let's get physical.

899
00:42:02.110 --> 00:42:06.130
With headbands and dancing and a boombox.

900
00:42:06.490 --> 00:42:08.350
Jenna, I worked in corporate America.

901
00:42:08.430 --> 00:42:13.750
I have been in human resources seminars that we had to go to.

902
00:42:13.930 --> 00:42:14.090
Yeah.

903
00:42:14.090 --> 00:42:16.350
I'm telling you, they had skits.

904
00:42:16.690 --> 00:42:17.130
What?

905
00:42:17.550 --> 00:42:23.070
When I watched this, I had such a flood of memories coming back of sitting in a tiny little

906
00:42:23.070 --> 00:42:25.430
conference room when I worked at this company.

907
00:42:25.730 --> 00:42:28.170
And our human resources department, there were two people.

908
00:42:28.370 --> 00:42:30.910
They would come in and act out skits of what's inappropriate.

909
00:42:30.910 --> 00:42:32.130
We had one guy.

910
00:42:32.470 --> 00:42:33.230
His name was Tom.

911
00:42:33.730 --> 00:42:35.110
And we had a gal.

912
00:42:35.370 --> 00:42:36.170
Her name was Susan.

913
00:42:36.350 --> 00:42:40.050
And he'd be like, Susan, that skirt looks really nice on you today.

914
00:42:40.550 --> 00:42:42.850
Hey, time to party.

915
00:42:42.850 --> 00:42:45.650
And then Susan would do a face like, huh?

916
00:42:46.430 --> 00:42:47.590
And then they'd freeze.

917
00:42:48.330 --> 00:42:51.290
And then Tom would say, what was inappropriate in this moment?

918
00:42:52.010 --> 00:42:56.390
And we'd all have to raise our hands and be like, he was kind of gross about her skirt.

919
00:42:56.970 --> 00:43:01.150
I only had to watch produced videos of weird things.

920
00:43:01.210 --> 00:43:03.310
I've never seen a live presentation.

921
00:43:03.710 --> 00:43:03.950
Oh, no.

922
00:43:04.050 --> 00:43:05.250
I watched skits.

923
00:43:05.670 --> 00:43:07.830
We had a fan question about this scene.

924
00:43:07.910 --> 00:43:08.390
We did.

925
00:43:08.390 --> 00:43:09.690
From Patricia B.

926
00:43:10.610 --> 00:43:16.230
She said, I'm wondering if some of the younger Office fans even know the song that Holly and

927
00:43:16.230 --> 00:43:17.170
Michael are performing.

928
00:43:17.730 --> 00:43:21.670
She wants to know, Angela, did your kids watch this one with you?

929
00:43:21.790 --> 00:43:23.890
Did you have to explain the song parody?

930
00:43:24.330 --> 00:43:25.510
Isabel watched it with me.

931
00:43:25.690 --> 00:43:27.370
She didn't ask about the song.

932
00:43:27.590 --> 00:43:28.450
She just thought it was funny.

933
00:43:28.690 --> 00:43:30.170
She probably thinks we made it up.

934
00:43:31.390 --> 00:43:36.550
Yeah, this was, I guess, for our younger listeners, a very famous song by Olivia Newton-John,

935
00:43:36.730 --> 00:43:37.450
Let's Get Physical.

936
00:43:37.910 --> 00:43:45.910
And the music video was like her in like an aerobics class singing and dancing with a

937
00:43:45.910 --> 00:43:46.490
headband.

938
00:43:46.990 --> 00:43:49.950
Jane Fonda had like these workout videos at the time, too.

939
00:43:50.050 --> 00:43:51.430
This was like a little trend.

940
00:43:51.690 --> 00:43:52.230
Oh, yeah.

941
00:43:52.390 --> 00:43:53.450
Sexy working out.

942
00:43:53.450 --> 00:44:01.510
But your sexy workout included tights, leg warmers, high tops, leotard, headband, wristband.

943
00:44:01.710 --> 00:44:01.970
Yeah.

944
00:44:02.270 --> 00:44:03.290
It was a whole thing.

945
00:44:03.390 --> 00:44:03.910
It was.

946
00:44:05.010 --> 00:44:06.470
I remember it well.

947
00:44:06.810 --> 00:44:12.110
Well, Holly begins her ethics meeting by explaining that there's been some misconduct.

948
00:44:12.110 --> 00:44:14.310
She's clearly talking about Ryan.

949
00:44:15.010 --> 00:44:16.590
Who's been hired again?

950
00:44:16.590 --> 00:44:18.390
It's so hilarious to me.

951
00:44:18.650 --> 00:44:19.450
I know.

952
00:44:20.150 --> 00:44:23.690
And then she starts going through the results of the quiz.

953
00:44:24.190 --> 00:44:24.350
Yeah.

954
00:44:24.730 --> 00:44:25.210
Pretty much.

955
00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:26.430
She's got this binder.

956
00:44:26.910 --> 00:44:27.270
Yeah.

957
00:44:27.390 --> 00:44:29.550
And she's got to go through the binder.

958
00:44:29.810 --> 00:44:30.950
The HR binder.

959
00:44:31.210 --> 00:44:31.370
Yeah.

960
00:44:31.750 --> 00:44:34.290
We had a fan question from Peyton M.

961
00:44:34.470 --> 00:44:40.070
In the conference room scene, did Creed and Meredith actually break when Stanley said the

962
00:44:40.070 --> 00:44:43.870
meeting was a waste of time or was it scripted for them to laugh?

963
00:44:44.110 --> 00:44:45.890
Well, I looked at the script.

964
00:44:46.230 --> 00:44:47.870
It was scripted.

965
00:44:47.870 --> 00:44:51.510
And the script said, people laugh a lot.

966
00:44:52.330 --> 00:44:54.570
That was the direction in the script.

967
00:44:55.030 --> 00:44:56.870
So the meeting isn't going so great.

968
00:44:57.010 --> 00:44:58.850
And Michael's like, you're losing them.

969
00:44:58.950 --> 00:44:59.210
Yeah.

970
00:44:59.550 --> 00:45:00.870
So he pulls Holly aside.

971
00:45:01.610 --> 00:45:02.950
You are losing them.

972
00:45:03.130 --> 00:45:04.470
They expect a lot.

973
00:45:05.010 --> 00:45:05.390
Yeah.

974
00:45:05.530 --> 00:45:06.370
It's really sweet.

975
00:45:06.390 --> 00:45:10.950
He's trying to help her in this meeting because he really wants her to succeed.

976
00:45:10.950 --> 00:45:14.190
So he says, let's get rid of the binder.

977
00:45:14.530 --> 00:45:18.650
This is your opportunity to speak up without any repercussions.

978
00:45:19.150 --> 00:45:23.090
He's like, guys, what are some things maybe you've done at work to waste time?

979
00:45:23.230 --> 00:45:23.630
What have you done?

980
00:45:23.730 --> 00:45:25.170
Anything or anything you want to share?

981
00:45:25.290 --> 00:45:25.390
Yeah.

982
00:45:25.530 --> 00:45:26.450
You have immunity.

983
00:45:27.030 --> 00:45:27.770
Go for it.

984
00:45:27.770 --> 00:45:34.990
Well, during this time, Michael confesses that he didn't work for five days when he discovered

985
00:45:34.990 --> 00:45:35.410
YouTube.

986
